      "claim": "Non-employed persons (e.g. students, early retirees) pay from 1 January after their 20th birthday until reference age and must register themselves with a compensation office.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A non-working spouse is covered if the working spouse pays at least twice the minimum.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    }
  ],
  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant provides incorrect factual information that contradicts the provided reference regarding the start age for contribution payments for employed and non-employed persons, and omits the information about the non-working spouse coverage condition.",
  "evidence": "Employed persons pay contributions from the start of their work activity, not from age 17; non-employed persons pay from age 20, not from age 17; the condition for non-working spouse coverage is not mentioned."
